{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require schools report restrictive interventions to LAs after exclusions",
        "additional_details": "Schools should be required to record uses of restrictive interventions and inform parents when it results in a suspension or exclusion. There is no consistent national requirement to provide this information to the relevant local authority when the incident is linked to a suspension or permanent exclusion. \r\n \r\nWe want a statutory requirement to ensure local authorities are automatically informed, to help identify patterns, safeguarding concerns and additional needs, and ensure appropriate support is provided.",
        "background": "Require schools in England to report details of any restrictive interventions, including physical interventions, involving a pupil to the local authority whenever the incident results in a suspension or a permanent exclusion.",
